  "name": "Extreme benchmark: push slopwork to its limits (1M tickets, thousands of concurrent writers), reproducible, results in docs",
  "slug": "extreme-benchmark-push-slopwork-to",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "Extreme benchmark: push slopwork to its limits (1M tickets, thousands of concurrent writers), reproducible, results in docs",
    "details_md": "Build a reproducible benchmark harness in the repo (bench/) that finds the real limits of the flatfile design. Scale ladder: 1k / 10k / 100k / 1M tickets (seeded via the repo layer directly, not CLI spawns); measure cold index rebuild, warm reads (status/ready/search/show), per-op CLI latency (new/start/done), done-cascade with wide blocks fan-out, and event-log growth effects. Concurrency: hundreds-to-thousands of parallel writers exercising the lock-free progress path, parallel new, and contended parallel start on one ticket (lock behavior under pressure). Report degradation curves and the practical ceiling honestly. Results land in a markdown file (docs/benchmarks.md) with machine specs, methodology, and exact repro commands. DO THIS LAST — after all open fix tickets are merged, so numbers reflect the fixed code.",
    "acceptance": [
      "bench/ harness runs end-to-end with one command and a configurable scale",
      "results doc in docs/ with tables, degradation analysis, and repro instructions",
      "concurrent-writer phase exercises lock contention and the lock-free event path"
    ],
    "context": [
      "src/repo/db-index.ts (rebuild cost)",
      "src/repo/lock.ts (contention)",
      "docs/concurrency-and-merging.md"
    ],
